{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-11T18:59:17.892Z","data":{"text":"I've completed task 2. Here's a summary.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Production code**\n- `src/core/web/web-events.ts` — `InvalidationHubOptions` gained optional `recordPath`. The hub watches it after the `treeWatchPaths` paths and treats a notification on it as a global invalidation (explicitly, plus via the existing outside-every-change path). `treeWatchPaths` is untouched; without `recordPath` the watched paths are identical to before.\n- `src/core/status/dispatch-watch.ts` — `watchDispatch` resolves `treeRecordPath(projectRoot, config)` exactly once in `startWatch`, before the first hub, stores it on the watch state, and every `openHub` passes it as `recordPath`. `refreshTrees` still compares `treeWatchPaths` alone.\n- `src/core/foundation/config-inbox.ts` — `DEFAULT_INBOX_CONFIG.pollSeconds` `30` → `300`.\n- `README.md` — the `--follow` paragraph now names osq's own git writes appending to `osq-trees.jsonl` in the repository's common git directory, which `--follow` and the dashboard watch; the `inbox.pollSeconds` line reads `300` and calls it the backstop for landings made outside osq.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/config-inbox.test.ts` — only the expected default changed `30` → `300`.\n- New `tests/dispatch-watch-tree-record.test.ts` — proves *Tree record watched* and *Tree record fires* with `scenario('status-inspection', …)` on a temporary repo with `vcs.enabled`/`vcs.author`, reusing the fake-watcher and manual-`every` patterns from `tests/dispatch-watch.test.ts` and counting `trees` seam calls. Nothing was added to `dispatch-watch.test.ts`.\n\n## The one judgement call\n\nThe living `openspec/specs/status-inspection/spec.md` has **two scenarios named \"Archived change that needs steering\"**, so `lookupScenario` refuses every status-inspection lookup. Since the living spec and the change delta are both outside scope, the new test builds a temporary lookup root from a copy of the real spec with that duplicate renamed (using the real delta while it exists) and points `OSQ_CHANGE` there for the file. The scenario text and THEN lines still come from the real spec/delta; no outcome is invented. This is documented under `## Deviated`, and the underlying living-spec defect under `## Outside scope` — it needs a future change to dedupe status-inspection so the accommodation can go away.\n\nBoth verifies pass: the task verify (37 tests) and `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, all tests, lint)."}}
